# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored.
#
# Every value here is read by scripts/deploy.mjs and nothing else. Shell
# variables win over the file, so a CI secret or an Ansible-supplied value
# overrides what is written down here.
#
# There is no browser half any more. These keys carried VITE_ twins while the
# admin SPA lived in this repo; the SPA is gone and so are the twins.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where to deploy, and the credential to do it with
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

HAPPYVIEW_URL=https://view.sharedcomputer.network

# Admin API key (hv_) from the HappyView dashboard. Needs permissions for
# lexicons, scripts, script variables, settings, and backfill.
#
# Minted by hand: HappyView offers no way to create one from Ansible or a CLI,
# so this is the manual step that keeps the registry outside the one-script
# rebuild. Script-deploy access is equivalent to authority over the registry
# (CLAUDE.md) — and, because db.raw has no read allowlist, to read access on
# HappyView's whole database. Guard it accordingly.
HAPPYVIEW_API_KEY=hv_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Script variables pushed to HappyView. Anything unset is skipped.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The service DID whose repo anchors the admin roster (public info).
SERVICE_DID=did:plc:xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Sole admin until a roster record exists, so the first roster can be written.
# An existing-but-empty roster still fails closed; this covers an ABSENT one.
BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_DID=did:plc:xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# The registry space. See "Bootstrap" in the README: creating it is the one
# step this repo cannot yet perform headlessly. Leave blank until it exists —
# deploy skips unset variables, so an early deploy is fine.
REGISTRY_SPACE_URI=

# Membership push. approve_member.lua and revoke_member.lua POST each grant
# and revocation here so the consumer can cache who is a member; leave both
# blank until that endpoint exists, and the notification is skipped. The
# registry stays the record either way — a push is a cache update, so a failed
# one is logged and never fails the approval.
#
# The token only authorises "assert a membership event". It cannot mint keys
# or read the registry, which is why a shared bearer is sufficient.
CORLISS_PUSH_URL=
CORLISS_PUSH_TOKEN=

# The service read door (syncMembers). A consumer rebuilt from nothing has
# witnessed no pushes, so it needs to read every grant and revocation back out
# of the space — at boot, with nobody signed in, which is why it cannot use the
# admin-authenticated listMembers. Blank means syncMembers refuses every call.
#
# Unlike the push token this one *reads*: a leak exposes the member roll — and,
# since XRPC dispatch is unauthenticated, to anyone anywhere rather than only to
# something on the cluster's network. It writes nothing and acts on no one's
# behalf, and it is deliberately a separate secret from CORLISS_PUSH_TOKEN so the
# two rotate independently.
#
# syncMembers is a QUERY, so this travels as a URL parameter: HappyView gates
# procedures behind DPoP auth, which a token-only caller cannot provide. Consumers
# should therefore call it over an internal address, keeping the token out of any
# edge or CDN log.
RECONCILE_TOKEN=
